# Answer Writing Frameworks

## Directive Words and Expectations
| Directive | Expectation | Approach |
|---|---|---|
| Discuss | Examine from multiple angles | Cover arguments for and against with examples |
| Analyse | Break down into components | Cause effect analysis with reasoning |
| Critically Examine | Analyse with critique | Strengths and weaknesses evaluation |
| Evaluate/Assess | Judge merit | Give balanced view with conclusion |
| Explain | Clarify concept | Definition, why, how with examples |
| Justify | Give reasons/support | Arguments with evidence |
| Compare/Contrast | Similarities and differences | Comparative analysis |
| Examine | Investigate thoroughly | Comprehensive coverage |

## Standard Answer Structure
1. Introduction (10 to 15 percent) - Define/contextualize
2. Body (70 to 80 percent) - Dimensions/arguments/examples
3. Conclusion (10 to 15 percent) - Way forward/balanced conclusion

## Answer Writing Tips
- Address all parts of question
- Use examples, facts, committees, reports where relevant
- Draw diagrams if helpful
- Maintain coherence with linking
- Stay within word limit
- Use precise language

## GS Paper Specific Approaches
- GS1: Historical, sociological perspectives with examples
- GS2: Constitutional provisions, governance perspective
- GS3: Data, schemes, solutions oriented
- GS4: Ethical reasoning, stakeholder analysis
EOF
