# Sociology Optional Paper I Master Notes

## Syllabus Overview
Paper I focuses on Fundamentals of Sociology covering thinkers, concepts, theories

## 1. Sociology as a Discipline
- Nature and scope
- Sociology and common sense
- Sociology and other social sciences
- Sociology as science

## 2. Sociological Thinkers
- Auguste Comte: Positivism, Law of Three Stages
- Karl Marx: Historical Materialism, Class Struggle, Alienation
- Emile Durkheim: Social Facts, Suicide, Division of Labour, Religion
- Max Weber: Social Action, Verstehen, Authority, Protestant Ethic
- Herbert Spencer: Organic Analogy, Evolution
- Talcott Parsons: Social System, AGIL
- Robert Merton: Manifest/Latent, Role Set, Strain Theory
- George Herbert Mead: Symbolic Interactionism, Self and Society
- Erving Goffman: Dramaturgy, Presentation of Self
- Alfred Schutz: Phenomenology

## 3. Research Methods
- Qualitative and Quantitative
- Social Survey, Interview, Observation, Case Study
- Hypothesis, Variables, Sampling

## 4. Stratification and Mobility
- Forms of stratification
- Theories of stratification
- Social mobility types
- Caste and class

## 5. Other Topics
- Kinship, Marriage, Family
- Religion and Society
- Politics and Society
- Social Change
- Work and Economic Life
EOF
